Dear Case Progression Team,

=20

I write regarding AC-2025-LON-004293 =E2=80=93 The King (on the application of Za=
hmoul) v Secretary of State for Justice & Ors, now sealed as of 1 December 2=
025.

=20

1. Request for confirmation that the permission stage will not be determine=
d on the papers

=20

For the avoidance of doubt, I respectfully request written confirmation tha=
t the permission stage will not be determined on the papers, given:
my diagnosed Autism Spectrum Condition and PTSD,
the signed medical report from Dr Bruce Hayse confirming clinical psychiatr=
ic risk,
and the fully engaged duties under:
=E2=80=A2 Equality Act 2010, ss.20=E2=80=9321 (reasonable adjustments),

=E2=80=A2 Public Sector Equality Duty, s.149,

=E2=80=A2 and the overriding objective concerning vulnerable litigants.

=20

A paper-only determination would be unsafe, discriminatory, and contrary to=
 the Court=E2=80=99s statutory duties.

=20

2. Open Justice and public listing

As the claim is now sealed, it is subject to the Open Justice principle and=
 CPR 5.4C.

I therefore ask the Court to ensure that the claim is listed for an oral he=
aring, and that no steps are taken on the papers unless I am able to partici=
pate effectively with reasonable adjustments.

=20

3. Urgent listing request (N463)

=20

My N463 urgent application =E2=80=94 filed 25 November and resubmitted with a ful=
ly ACO-compliant bundle on 1 December =E2=80=94 remains outstanding. I respectfull=
y request that this now be placed before a judge for urgent consideration.

=20

4. Confirmation requested

=20

May I please have confirmation of:
The next procedural step for this claim
Whether the urgent N463 has now been referred to a judge
Assurance that no paper-only decision will be made
=20

Given the medical evidence and the safeguarding concerns identified by my t=
reating physician, timely progression is essential.

Thank you for your assistance.

=20

Yours faithfully,

Nadia Zahmoul

Litigant in Person

Email: nadia@rosekross.com


--B_3852819906_4157833100
